+# Integrate the published bank/telephone tranche
+
+October26,2026. User instruction: include the findings published in AveLyra
+commit bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2 in the investigation.
+
+Scope: integrate all BP01-BP10 findings, not only the short announcement;
+distinguish original carrier material, FBI analysis, interview recollection,
+party descriptions and remaining roots. Preserve every conflicting value and
+the positive eight-call sample. Do not turn any conflict into an actor/intent
+finding or claim independent corroboration from repeated source accounts.
+
+Deliver an integration report and structured crosswalk; update the current
+five-bundle record targets and research navigation; preserve the preceding
+source report, ledger and target files unchanged. Save a byte-exact snapshot of
+the fifteen published files, check it against the Git commit and live GitHub
+blob IDs, and record the exact author/committer and publication scope.
+
+The 1A reference concerns apartment payment documents. It does not locate or
+close the separate July2003 $100,000 informant-payment voucher target.
+June23,2000 AT&T billing records do not supply the February4 cellular returns.
+Printed rows, billing units, unique calls and speakers must remain separate.
+
+Acceptance: all10 BP IDs and10 BPR targets accounted for; S007/S013 and BR01
+links explicit; other four operational bundles retain their unresolved status;
+old source records byte-identical; exact text diff against preceding navigation
+and target versions; actual verification commands/results. No new raw personal
+data, case facts, litigation records, outreach, fees or private push.
+
+This is a local research integration of an already published source tranche.
+Do not represent the previous operational-source follow-up as publicly published
+or claim this integration itself was committed/pushed without doing so.
