+| [BP09](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2/investigation/broader-evidence/bank-phone-records-2026-10-26/RECORD.md#L199) | Rental-manager account, payment-component/office-visit differences, a $1,010 payment, a copying/re-stapling concern and explicit **1A-section** attachment custody lead are retained. | Supplemental1 physical161-163, EO14040-003828-003830; averment section1638. $775+$8 insurance+$775 differs from the application-fee description; alone versus accompanied accounts need originals. Witness inference about document handling is not forensic proof of tampering. |
+| [BP10](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/bb9e9c5d6fd30ec3bb3fbc5359f388ef8c8c0db2/investigation/broader-evidence/bank-phone-records-2026-10-26/RECORD.md#L227) | A July18,2007 EC names a **42-page frequency spreadsheet and i2 charts**; the entire named enclosure has not been separately verified. | Part5 physical75-76, EO14040-002797-002798; averment sections756-759. The analysis/graphics are not additional independent carrier records. S013's incomplete `02/2000` day remains unknown. |
+
+## Confirming evidence is retained alongside discrepancies
+
+BP08 supports one FBI report against an actual carrier sample. That matters to
+our own evaluation: a register containing only mismatches would misdescribe the
+reviewed evidence. It does not establish accuracy of every FBI analysis or
+resolve separate dates, repayment descriptions or22/27 units.
+
+This integration reran the published recount against its hash-pinned403-page
+FBI source. It reproduced67 rows overall and27 within the specified window,
+split21/6 across the labelled lines. It also checked the preserved carrier
+transcription's8 rows, six/two destinations and42 billed minutes. This second
+check is arithmetic on the published transcription, not a fresh visual or
+carrier-authentication examination. The underlying sample visual check remains
+attributed to the original bank/telephone study.
+
+## The 1A lead does not close the informant-payment track
+
+The 1A passage concerns **Parkwood apartment-payment documents and ledgers**.
+The next useful target is the attachment list and 1A inventory for the
+October28,2001 rental-manager interview, together with its actual payment
+attachments, originals/copies and custody records.
+
+This is separate from **BR04**, the July2003 **$100,000 informant payment**.
+No voucher or purpose for that payment has been located through the apartment
+record. BR04 remains open. Nor does a witness's suspicion that apartment records
+were copied establish who handled them, why, or whether anything was altered.
+
+## Current next records
+
+All ten published **BPR01-BPR10** targets are carried verbatim into
+targets-v2.json with their scope and limitations. The first acquisitions remain:
+
+1. Plaintiffs Ex550/FBI8057 opening-deposit receipt and account-opening material.
+2. KSA Ex91/FBI2808-09, original cash entry/check images and debit/credit ledger.
+3. Teller interview/worksheets referenced at EO14040-002738; both2002 FBI originals.
+4. Parkwood payment attachments and the specific1A inventory/custody chain.
+5. Ex12A and source February4 cellular returns, subscriber attribution, original
+   time fields and the selection/deduplication rules behind22 versus27.
+
+April19/20 carrier rows, the42-page enclosure, complete AT&T return/account
+linkage and the full2003 interview/deposition editions remain in that target
+set. No pending record was silently removed because another record was found.
+
+## Publication, preservation and limits
+
+The existing public commit's author/committer and all15 GitHub file blob IDs
+were checked against the Git snapshot and local reviewed copies through the
+documented AveLyra profile. That verifies the cited publication, not a new push
+of this integration. The full old operational report, eight RF records, original
+target ledger and first-tranche source findings remain unchanged.
+
+The integration is research rather than a promotion to legal facts or pleading
+authority. It does not establish conversational content, attack foreknowledge,
+participation, deliberate record alteration or a demolition connection.
+Conflicting values remain unresolved, and same-source repetition is not
+independent corroboration. [Requirement checklist](CHECKLIST.json) and
+[text changes](diffs/integration.diff) preserve revision accountability.
