+      "verbatim_published_body": "\nThe declassified Joint Inquiry, **printed p.422, footnote 1; physical PDF p.13**, places\ntwo FBI accounts alongside one another. Its quotation of a **November 18, 2002\nresponse, p.3**, says an equal cash deposit on the check date suggests reimbursement.\nIts quotation of an **October 14, 2002 document** says there was no bank\ndocumentation supporting reimbursement from Hazmi or Mihdhar. We acquired the\ncongressional reproduction, not those two underlying FBI originals.\n[Joint Inquiry release](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-Y4_IN8_18-PURL-gpo71223/pdf/GOVPUB-Y4_IN8_18-PURL-gpo71223.pdf#page=13)\n\nA **July 21, 2004 FBI EC**, **EO14040-002738; physical p.16**, describes a $1,558\ncashier's check, an equal cash **deposit**, and the $9,900 account opening, all posted\nwithin seven minutes on February 4, 2000. It reports teller corroboration; the\nreference identifying the teller interview is redacted. This is the FBI's account\nof the records and corroboration, not our independent bank/teller examination.\n[FBI Part 5](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file#page=16)\n\nThe OIG's same-day repayment account and the 2025 court's repayment finding remain\nbeside these records. Neither repetition supplies the missing transaction images.\nThe court cites **KSA Ex91, FBI2808\u201309**, not plaintiffs' Ex91 (Ratchford declaration).\n[OIG chapter 5, notes128\u2013129](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm)\n\u00b7 [2025 opinion, p.21](https://www.nysd.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2025-08/03-md-01570%2011182.pdf#page=21)\n\n**Open test:** obtain both dated FBI documents, the original credit/debit ledger,\ncash deposit/check images and teller statement. Equal amounts alone do not identify\nthe person who supplied cash. No