+      "verbatim_published_body": "\nThe released **August 4\u20136, 2003 Bayoumi interview FD-302**, transcribed August 18,\n**continuation p.5, physical p.11, Bates000002669**, records his uncertain estimate\nthat the men possessed **$4,000\u2013$8,000**. Later records describe a **$9,900 cash\nopening deposit**. The original receipt identified as **plaintiffs Ex550/FBI8057**\nhas not been acquired here. The interview and reported receipt concern differently\ndescribed quantities and different levels of certainty; retain both without turning\nthe mismatch into a finding of lying.\n[Released interview](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-investigation-2003-09-sep/at_download/file#page=11)\n\nA 2024 Motley Rice news account attributes nearly $10,000 transferred into their\naccount to Bayoumi. Its own public averment \u00a71637 instead describes Mihdhar's cash\ndeposit; the court p.21 also attributes the cash deposit to the hijackers. These\ndescriptions are preserved, not equated. A bank companion, cash depositor and\nultimate source of funds are separate propositions.\n[News account, extracted block B056](https://www.motleyrice.com/news/september-11-2001-new-evidence-23-years-later)\n\u00b7 [Averment \u00a71637, physical p.416](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/20240802%20Redacted%20public%20averment.pdf#page=416)\n\n**Open test:** receipt, account-opening documents and cash-origin evidence. The\n$9,900 amount alone does not establish intent to evade reporting requirements.\n",
