+      "verbatim_published_body": "\nThe **September 29, 2005 FBI telephone-analysis EC**, **EO14040-002752; physical p.30,\nprinted p.5**, places the bank visit approximately **15:30\u201315:40** and prints:\n\n| Time as printed | From label | To label | Duration as printed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|16:40|BAYOUMI Cell|AULAQI Home|1:00|\n|16:42|BAYOUMI Cell|AR-RIBAT PAYPHONE|1:00|\n|16:43|BAYOUMI Cell|AR-RIBAT FAX|1:00|\n|16:52|ALTHUMAIRY (CBR)|BAYOUMI Cell|1:00|\n|16:55|BAYOUMI Cell|ALTHUMAIRY (CBR)|2:00|\n\nThis is an original FBI **analysis table**, not the carrier return for those calls.\nIts later discussion states that the calls' significance is unknown because their\ncontent is unavailable. It also records Bayoumi's denial of introductions while\noffering introductions as an investigative possibility.\n[Table](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file#page=30)\n\u00b7 [limits, EO14040-002759/p.37](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file#page=37)\n\nThe averment \u00a71639 calls the 16:55 destination Thumairy's **cell phone**; the FBI\ntable calls it **CBR**, and EO14040-002757 describes that number as a can-be-reached\nnumber subscribed to someone else. Preserve both descriptions; the carrier and\nsubscriber evidence needed to map them is still missing. A fax/payphone label does\nnot identify a particular human speaker.\n[Averment \u00a71639/p.416](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/20240802%20Redacted%20public%20averment.pdf#page=416)\n\u00b7 [number definitions, FBI p.35](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file#page=35)\n\n**Open test:** plaintiffs Ex12A, Ex5 p.197 and their underlying Sprint/local-carrier\nreturns; mapping/subscriber documents, direction, timezone, billing units and\nduplicate-record rules. Timing is a testable lead; conversational purpose is not\nestablished by proximity to the bank visit.\n",
