+      "verbatim_published_body": "\nThe FBI table **EO14040-002757\u2013002759, physical pp.35\u201337** says **67 contacts** for\nDecember 16, 1998\u2013December 20, 2000. A reproducible extraction counts **67 printed dated\nrows**. In the inclusive December 6, 1999\u2013February 4, 2000 window it counts **27 rows**:\n**21** involving BAYOUMI#2 and **6** involving BAYOUMI#4. The averment **\u00a7\u00a71641\u20131643**\nuses **22 calls** for that window. Both counts and the unsupplied selection rule\nare preserved. No subset is asserted to explain the pleading's total.\n[FBI table](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-part-5/at_download/file#page=35)\n\u00b7 [Averment \u00a7\u00a71641\u20131643, physical pp.416\u2013417](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/20240802%20Redacted%20public%20averment.pdf#page=416)\n\n[CALL-ROWS.json](CALL-ROWS.json) preserves every printed row and its extracted-text\nline; [recount_calls.py](recount_calls.py) reproduces the count from the pinned PDF.\nRows are not automatically unique conversations: matching two endpoints, repeated\nentries and carrier billing conventions require checks. No statistical claim of\nan unusually dense call cluster is made without comparable coverage and baseline.\n\nKSA's public reply disputes shared-line attribution and the proposed call-circle\ninference. Preserve this adversarial account alongside the plaintiffs' account;\nneither is a carrier record. The 2025 court made substantive jurisdiction findings,\nbut reserved merits/credibility determinations; this review does not erase that.\n[KSA reply, printed p.15/physical p.29 n.8](https://www.motleyrice.com/sites/default/files/documents/AT_HR/9-11/Docket%20%23%209795%20-%20Redacted%20Public%20Version%20%20KSA%20REPLY%20MOL%20ISO%20%5B9368%5D%20MTN%20to%20Dismiss%20%28Prev.%20filed%2