+      "verbatim_published_body": "\nThe FBI's **2(c)/2(d) supplemental release1** contains:\n\n- **EO14040-003831; physical p.164:** January 7, 2002 FD-302 saying AT&T toll records\n  were entered on December 27, 2001; it describes eight calls on June 23, 2000.\n- **EO14040-003832; p.165:** data-loading request with originals-attached marked\n  yes, assigned December 27 and completed December 28, 2001.\n- **EO14040-003833; p.166:** AT&T November 29, 2001 subpoena-return letter describing\n  **two accounts for one number**, enclosed account/toll material and an **18-month**\n  retention period. This records the carrier's statement, not independent legal\n  verification of its retention-law claim or proof about other carriers.\n- **EO14040-003865 and003867; pp.198,200:** July 4, 2000 bill usage summary and actual\n  carrier call-detail page: **eight June 23 rows, six to Saudi Arabia and two to the\n  UK, total42 billed minutes**. This agrees with the FD-302's count/date/destination\n  description. Recipient/account numbers are redacted and are not republished.\n- **EO14040-003884; p.217:** a separate July 27, 1998 carrier call-detail page, showing\n  that the public packet includes earlier original billing material too. It is not\n  joined to the July 2000 account through redacted identifiers.\n\n[Carrier return and loading trail](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-2-d-supplemental-release-1/at_download/file#page=164)\n\u00b7 [Original call detail](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11-attacks-investigation-and-related-materials/9-11-material-released-in-response-to-executive-order-14040/documents-responsive-to-executive-order-14040-2-c-2-d-supplemental-release-1/at_download/file#page=200)\n\nThis is a positive source check within one evidentiary chain, not independent\ncorroboration by multiple witnesses. It does not authenticate the